>> llply(state_seats, function(x) print(x))
>> ## or somewhat more verbose in output,
>> ## llply(state_seats, print)
>>
>> Basic idea:
>>
>>  * Combine the input data sets into a list.
>>  * Write a single function that outputs a ggplot object for an
>> arbitrary input data frame.
>>  * Use a **ply family function to recursively generate the ggplot
>> objects from the components of the input list; save to another list
>> object.
>>  * Use another **ply family function to print it.
>>
>> At a basic level, there is no concept of 'pointers' in R (they exist,
>> but matter only when doing advanced programming). The above is more
>> the 'R-way' of doing things - the SAS analogue would be the BY
>> statement.
