On Tue, Feb 5, 2013 at 3:26 PM, Hermann Norpois <hnor...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hello,
>
> freqduzin.df is a frequency-table generated via table(). And I have no
> problems to plot my data, for instance by
>
> ggplot (freqduzin.df)+geom_point (aes (x=duzin.sum, y=Freq))
>
> But I would like to have bars and I dont find a way. I assume I dont
> understand geom_bar or geom_histogram. Can anybody give me a hint?

geom_bar transforms the data by default. Since your data doesn't need
to be transformed, you have to tell it not to do that:

ggplot (freqduzin.df)+geom_bar(aes(x=duzin.sum, y=Freq), stat="identity")

Best,
Ista

