Subject: ggplot2: change background colour, depending on factor levels on a discrete x axis
Message-ID: <PzlYPK9rYaY.2rjFqfGSWFUJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/PzlYPK9rYaY/m/2rjFqfGSWFUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,

I have been trying to find a way in which I can partition the background of a plot into different sections depending on my factor levels.

I found this post: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9968975/using-ggplot2-in-r-how-do-i-make-the-background-of-a-graph-different-colours-in

in which they manage to do what I want for a continuous x axis, though I have not been able to apply this to my discrete x. If anyone has an idea of how to do it, I would greatly appreciate to get to know it.

Thanks!!

From uf4249b01b99d0091 at groups.google.com  Thu Feb 21 12:00:05 2013
From: uf4249b01b99d0091 at groups.google.com (Ben Bond-Lamberty)
Date: Thu, 21 Feb 2013 12:00:05 +0000
Subject: Re: ggplot2: change background colour, depending on factor levels on a discrete x axis
Message-ID: <PzlYPK9rYaY.MKrq6oXNJPEJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <PzlYPK9rYaY.2rjFqfGSWFUJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <PzlYPK9rYaY.2rjFqfGSWFUJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/PzlYPK9rYaY/m/MKrq6oXNJPEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You should be able to use geom_rect, as that stackoverflow example
shows, but with a couple tweaks:

d <- data.frame(x=c("A","B","C"),y=c(1,2,3))

ggplot(d,aes(x,y)) +geom_blank() +
geom_rect(aes(xmin=as.numeric(x)-.5,xmax=as.numeric(x)+.5,ymin=-Inf,ymax=Inf,fill=x))
+ geom_bar(stat="identity")

Ben

